y hand strength is overall mediocre (missing Jokers and holding only one 2).\n\nReason: Using the 3333 bomb on the very first turn to stop a mid-sized straight is generally a poor trade, especially when my hand lacks a strong follow-up sequence to seize control of the game. The Landlord likely holds strong cards (Jokers, 2s) to defend their bid. It is strategically better to preserve the bomb for a high-value threat (like stopping a 2 or a final play) or to support the teammate later. Passing allows the teammate a chance to intervene if they have a straight, and keeps my defensive option open for a more critical moment.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
